<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: for, indexing,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function constructs a directed graph structure from a given set of vertices and edges. It also computes the graph properties listed in the output details below.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>vertices</pf> (n x 1, integer) integer — : A list of vertex IDs.</p>
			<p><pf>edges</pf> (m x 2 or m x 3, integer) integer — : A list of edges where each row contains the starting and ending vertex IDs.</p>
			<p><pf>graph_name</pf> (string) number — : A name for the graph stored as part of the output structure.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>G</pf> (struct) number — : A structure representing the graph containing the following fields:</p>
			<p><pf>G.name</pf> (string) number — : The name of the graph as provided in <pf>graph_name</pf>.</p>
			<p><pf>G.vertices</pf> (n x 1, integers) integer — : List of vertex index IDs</p>
			<p><pf>G.edges</pf> (m x 3) number — : A matrix where each row represents an edge connecting two vertices.</p>
			<p><pf>G.n</pf> (integer) integer — : The number of vertices in the graph.</p>
			<p><pf>G.m</pf> (integer) integer — : The number of edges in the graph.</p>
			<p><pf>G.adj_mat</pf> (n x n double array) double — : The adjacency matrix of the graph.</p>
			<p><pf>G.cost_mat</pf> (n x n double array) double — : The cost/weight matrix of the graph.</p>
			<p><pf>G.out_degrees</pf> (n x 1, integers) number — : List of vertex out-degrees.</p>
			<p><pf>G.in_degrees</pf> (n x 1, integers) number — : List of vertex in-degrees.</p>
			<p><pf>HW6P1</pf> number — Note: The values of the fields 6 through 9 should come from the output of <pf>HW6P1</pf> - <pf>HW6P4</pf>, respectively.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>If the edges matrix is input without weights (i.e., a 3rd column), give each edge a default weight of 1.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
